WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.780
Finally here at our little news program

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.450
we love to look forward to the next generation of newsers.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.160
And in that spirit, we have a very special guest.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.350
She is a budding young journalist from Idaho Falls

5
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:17.740
who's becoming an internet sensation for her interviews.

6
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.400
She's interviewed her mom, her dad, her neighbors,

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.620
Keith Morrison, Lester Holt, Dr. Oz!

8
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.220
Oh my gosh!

9
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.951
She is a rising star and today, guess what?

10
00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:33.650
Rossy we get to join that illustrious list.

11
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:34.920
I'm so honored.

12
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.520
Please welcome seven year old

13
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.520
behind the Seven Questions with Emmy,

14
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.652
Emmy Eaton!

15
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:41.619
Emmy!

16
00:00:41.619 --> 00:00:42.980
(audience applauding)

17
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:43.813
Hi.

18
00:00:45.961 --> 00:00:48.960
I'm so excited to be talking with you guys today.

19
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.930
Oh my goodness.

20
00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.980
Emmy, you've done over 40 interviews

21
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.099
and you've got such a natural talent.

22
00:00:56.099 --> 00:01:01.099
What is it about interviewing that you like so much?

23
00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.050 line:15%
I like that I get to talk

24
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.020 line:15%
to so many people that are so amazing

25
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.921 line:15%
and I love asking questions.

26
00:01:07.921 --> 00:01:10.070
Do you do research?

27
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.750
Do you pick your subjects?

28
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.330
What's your process?

29
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.240
Well, I think of what they do.

30
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.469
Like if I were interviewing an author,

31
00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:21.480
I would think, "Oh, what book did they write?"

32
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.831
And I would ask about that.

33
00:01:22.831 --> 00:01:26.082
And if they wrote a fantasy, I would say,

34
00:01:26.082 --> 00:01:28.578
"Okay, why did you want to write a fantasy?"

35
00:01:28.578 --> 00:01:30.080
I love it.

36
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.610
Have you always been curious your whole entire life?

37
00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.671
Yes, I've been very curious.

38
00:01:34.671 --> 00:01:37.360
That's why you're a good journalist, Emmy.

39
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.091
Is there a story that you would like

40
00:01:39.091 --> 00:01:43.113
for everyone to hear today that you feel is important?

41
00:01:44.379 --> 00:01:49.379
There was this person, he lives in Rexburg.

42
00:01:49.511 --> 00:01:54.140
He made an igloo, they call it the Skittle igloo.

43
00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.057
They put pans of ice and then they add food coloring

44
00:01:58.057 --> 00:02:00.670
and they stuck it on the igloo.

45
00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.290 line:15%
They're the [Inaudible].

46
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.080 line:15%
They put lights in, so it looks really cool at night.

47
00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.790 line:15%
And the dad's a doctor.

48
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.130 line:15%
So everyday after delivering a baby,

49
00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.429
he would get back to working on the igloo.

50
00:02:12.429 --> 00:02:16.250
Okay, Emmy, I just wish you the very best

51
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.580
and I want you to go out there

52
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.237
and keep asking the important questions,

53
00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:23.200
showing the fun things that are happening in life.

54
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.500
And most importantly, would you come back and visit us?

55
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.333
Yeah.

56
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:28.230
Okay good.

57
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.270 line:15%
I'm so glad, we need more of Emmy.

58
00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.810 line:15%
The world needs more Emmy.

59
00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.317 line:15%
Thank you so much for coming today.

60
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:38.900 line:15%
(upbeat music)

